# EAS reads this file from the app directory in a monorepo.
**/node_modules/
**/.expo/
**/dist/
**/dist-verify/
**/dist-verify2/
**/web-build/
**/dist-release-check/
.git/

# Unrelated monorepo projects and release material.
/staff-app/
/tmp/
/public/
/src/
/supabase/
/whatsapp-bot/
/old whatsapp bots/
/store-assets/
/poster-output/
/deliverables/
/docs/
/scripts/
/tools/
/.github/

# --- Monorepo release material, excluded RECURSIVELY ---
#
# These were previously listed only as root-anchored paths (/deliverables/),
# but EAS evaluates the per-app .easignore from the app directory, where a
# leading slash means the app folder and not the repo root. So none of them
# matched and every build uploaded a 255 MB archive: deliverables is 408 MB,
# public 90 MB, tmp 54 MB, store-assets 17 MB. That is not merely slow — a
# 1.1.5 APK build died at 102 MB of 255 MB with write ECONNRESET, because the
# bigger the upload the likelier it is to be reset.
#
# Only names that do NOT exist inside an app folder are globbed. `src`,
# `scripts` and `assets` are deliberately absent from this list: staff-app has
# all three, and `**/src/` would exclude the app's own source.
**/deliverables/
**/public/
**/tmp/
**/store-assets/
**/poster-output/
**/output/
**/docs/
**/tools/
**/supabase/
**/whatsapp-bot/
**/old whatsapp bots/
